    "details": {
      "alignment": "Unaligned",
      "type": {
        "value": "construct",
        "subtype": "Fawful-Bot"
      },
      "cr": 0.5,
      "biography": {
        "value": "<p><em>Fawful's Forces packet sheet — Chortle-Bot.</em> Built by <code>tools/build-forge-packets.py</code> from the NPC Forge roster <code>data/forge/fawfuls-forces.json</code> (entry <code>chortle-bot</code>): Small construct (Fawful-Bot), Unaligned; CR 1/2 (proficiency +2, to hit +4 with DEX); AC 13 (tin plating), hit points 18 (4d6+4), speed 30 ft.. A GM scene kit for the Fawful's Forces article's present (1040 BF), not a filed event; the faction article stays the authority.</p><p>The cheapest thing Fawful builds and the thing he builds most of. A Chortle-Bot is a tin bean on legs with a laugh-capacitor where a mind should be: it giggles when it walks, giggles when it stabs, and giggles loudest when a dozen of them have found something to stab together. The faction article's Fury Meter puts \"Fawful-Bots\" on the third rung, after the minions and the traps — these are the first Fawful-Bots, the ones the occupation turns loose in the castle's corridors by the crate.</p><p>Alone, one is a nuisance that a Palace Guard can kick over. The danger is the chorus — three or more within ten feet of each other start timing their swings to the laugh — and the burst at the end, which has cost more than one careless boot a toe. The wind-up key is the joke Fawful never fixed: he thinks nobody will get close enough to use it.</p><p><strong>Role:</strong> swarm skirmisher · <strong>tier:</strong> Fawful-Bot · <strong>folder:</strong> Fawful's Furious Freaks / Machines of Fury.</p><h3>Art</h3><p>Token plate <code>portraits/fawfuls-forces/chortle-bot.png</code> — NPC Forge render, seed 410001, cut from a flat #FF00FF field. Prompt: <q>Clean cel-shaded cartoon character art in the style of Mario &amp; Luigi RPG concept art, bold dark outlines, flat colours, simple shading. A small round lime-green tin robot shaped like a bean with a huge toothy grin, two round yellow glowing eyes, a brass wind-up key in its back, short stubby brass legs and arms, holding a sparking brass prod. Full body, whole figure visible, three-quarter view, centred, isolated on a plain flat solid magenta background (#FF00FF), no floor, no ground shadow, no text, no border.</q></p>",
        "public": ""
      },
